{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"09d27a55e23f0042ba096ed63e33a748cb4e944e664ac5e7d437375198cfe694","digest":{"component_or_area":"doctor command - mapping diagnostics","key_entities":["rebar doctor","mapping_config.load_mapping_config","MappingConfigError","mapping_probe.build_probe","effective_status_map","effective_type_map","effective_link_map","assert_type_decisions_complete","config.projects","jira-datacenter","capability_installed","JIRA_PAT","resolve_jira_datacenter_settings","src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","docs/user-guide.md"],"problem_keywords":["mapping configuration diagnostics","offline validation","live drift detection","Jira compatibility","portability","graceful degradation"],"propositions":["Offline mapping diagnostics must detect load-time failures (non-integer hierarchy, malformed blocks) and resolve-time errors (out-of-vocabulary values, unmapped non-skipped entries) via stdlib-only config resolvers without importing jira adapters, yielding error findings with verbatim MappingConfigError details and non-zero exit.","Live-drift checking must be best-effort and degrade gracefully: when jira-datacenter extra is absent, credentials unset, settings resolution fails, or probe transport times out (bounded by doctor-side wall-clock timeout), emit a single unavailable finding with reason and return success.","Empty projects config blocks (stubs) must be surfaced as warning findings, not errors, preserving non-zero exit only for actual validation failures.","Mapping diagnostics findings must be stored in a separate list from blocking-edge scan findings, rendered independently, and kept out of run_repair iteration to preserve existing doctor.scan() contract.","Live-drift detection must compare configured vocabulary against observed Jira values for status, type, and link axes via the reused read-only mapping_probe, emitting one finding per divergence; hierarchy divergence detection is excluded by design (Data Center probe never observes hierarchyLevel).","The mapping diagnostics implementation must remain portable: execute where jira-datacenter extra is absent and no credentials are set, with offline checks always running and live-drift gracefully unavailable."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787500754974557001,"uuid":"73fe1da9-df05-465a-9f0c-4e61601407b1"}